I return from the clinic to my quiet flat.
I am tired.
I go to the kitchen and take a glass of water.
I take my first dose of medicine.
Just then, someone knocks on the door.
I open the door.
Outside, my neighbor Asha and her dog Moti are standing.
Asha asks, "Maya, how is your health?"
I say, "My health is not fine, Asha."
"I have a bad pain in my head and I have a severe cold."
Moti looks at me and wags his tail.
I smile and say, "Moti, how are you?"
Asha asks, "What did the doctor say?"
I answer, "It is just a viral infection."
Asha says, "Maya, you should rest."
"You should drink a lot of warm water."
I say, "Yes, I am going to sleep now."
Asha says, "Alright, if you need anything, tell me."
They both leave and I close the door.
I lie down on my bed and close my eyes.
